From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Release the external displays once the splash is gone, not
 before sddm

omarchy-mac-external-displays.service was ordered after plymouth-quit and
plymouth-quit-wait and before display-manager.service/sddm.service. With
Omarchy's Plymouth handover (omacom/omarchy plymouth-handover d7feacb59) sddm
starts first and only deactivates Plymouth; Hyprland quits it through
omarchy-plymouth-quit.service once it has the display. The release then sat
between the two: sddm waited for the release, the release for
plymouth-quit-wait, which waits for Plymouth to exit, which waits for the
compositor sddm starts. Nothing moved until the handover's 60 s timer quit
Plymouth (J604 boot 7ce7196f: timer 85.75 s, release 85.86 s, sddm 85.89 s,
Hyprland 87.07 s, passphrase at 23.60 s).

The release keeps waiting for the splash to be gone in both boots:
plymouth-quit-wait finishes only when plymouthd has exited, whoever quit
it, and omarchy-plymouth-quit.service joins plymouth-quit.service in its
After=. It is no longer ordered before the display manager. Its synthetic
hotplug already exists for a compositor that is up: aquamarine enables its
udev monitor before it scans the GPUs (src/backend/drm/DRM.cpp,
CSession::attempt before scanGPUs), so a release that lands before, during
or after Hyprland's first scan is seen. Without the handover the order is
unchanged up to sddm: plymouth-quit runs before sddm as before, and the
release now runs beside sddm's start instead of in front of it.

Tests: the unit orders or pulls in nothing besides its After= list.

No first-boot drop-in for omarchy-plymouth-quit.service: stock
omarchy-settings ships no such unit, so it would order nothing.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 omarchy-mac-boot/README.md                    |  2 +-
 .../lib/omarchy/mac-boot/external-displays    |  9 ++++-----
 .../omarchy-mac-external-displays.service     | 19 +++++++++++++------
 .../test/mac-external-displays-test.sh        |  9 ++++++---
 4 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/omarchy-mac-boot/README.md b/omarchy-mac-boot/README.md
index a097894..6525e8b 100644
--- a/omarchy-mac-boot/README.md
+++ b/omarchy-mac-boot/README.md
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ It covers what stays on an installed Mac and runs again when the Mac updates. Wh
 
 `install DESTDIR` stages commands in `/usr/bin`, sourced modules/setup leaves in `/usr/lib/omarchy-mac/boot`, the lifecycle dispatch entrypoints in `entrypoints/` in `/usr/lib/omarchy/mac-boot`, and the initramfs, in-place encryption and first-boot payload in `files/` at its installed paths (mkinitcpio drop-ins, initcpio hooks, units, presets, the ALPM hooks and `/etc/default/update-m1n1`, which pins update-m1n1's device-tree order to the C locale). One ALPM hook rebuilds the initramfs when a drop-in changes; `11-omarchy-mac-saved-modules.hook` runs right after kernel-modules-hook puts the running kernel's modules back and, only after a kernel downgrade, moves them to `/usr/lib/modules/.old` as `linux-modules-cleanup` would at the next boot, so update-m1n1's `-ARCH` default gives m1n1 the installed kernel's device trees. It performs no live setup. Its presets and first-boot hand-off never enable `speakersafetyd`: omarchy-mac's `80-omarchy-mac-audio.preset` (#535) is its only owner, and an upgrade leaves existing enable links alone. A boot pin must therefore not publish ahead of an omarchy-mac pin that includes #535: until then no edge package presets speakersafetyd, and the image check refuses an image without it enabled. The recipe's `backup=` covers every `files/etc` path and `files/usr/lib/omarchy/initcpio`. `test/all` runs command fixtures and the payload's offline checks; `OMARCHY_DISPOSABLE_BOOT_TESTS=1` also builds real initramfs images and converts loop-device disks in privileged containers. Shared provisioning and reset integration is covered by `test/integration/` at the repository root, against the Omarchy runtime.
 
-While first boot keeps the splash up, a laptop with its lid open shows it on the built-in screen only: `70-omarchy-mac-external-displays.rules` has `/usr/lib/omarchy/mac-boot/external-displays hold` force the Apple display card's external connectors off as the card appears, before Plymouth sees it. The lid is read from the kernel's lid switch (`/usr/lib/omarchy/mac-boot/lid-state`), since the card can appear before logind starts. Nothing is held on a shut or unknown lid, a desktop Mac or once the splash is over. `omarchy-mac-external-displays.service` turns them back on after Plymouth quits and owner setup or a password reset on tty1 ends, before the display manager starts, with a synthetic hotplug so the compositor rescans them. A held display may wake to a black console rather than stay asleep (the kernel console can light it before the hold), and a boot that never reaches multi-user.target keeps it off.
+While first boot keeps the splash up, a laptop with its lid open shows it on the built-in screen only: `70-omarchy-mac-external-displays.rules` has `/usr/lib/omarchy/mac-boot/external-displays hold` force the Apple display card's external connectors off as the card appears, before Plymouth sees it. The lid is read from the kernel's lid switch (`/usr/lib/omarchy/mac-boot/lid-state`), since the card can appear before logind starts. Nothing is held on a shut or unknown lid, a desktop Mac or once the splash is over. `omarchy-mac-external-displays.service` turns them back on once Plymouth is gone, whoever quit it (`plymouth-quit.service`, or Omarchy's Plymouth handover from the compositor), and owner setup or a password reset on tty1 ends, with a synthetic hotplug so a running display manager or compositor rescans them. It is not ordered before the display manager: with the handover, Plymouth quits only after the display manager's compositor has the display. A held display may wake to a black console rather than stay asleep (the kernel console can light it before the hold), and a boot that never reaches multi-user.target keeps it off.
 
 The Limine menu is Omarchy's, timeout and quiet mode included: `setup/limine-boot.sh` keeps the template's, and `/usr/lib/omarchy/mac-boot/limine-menu-defaults` gives a menu that still carries the `timeout: 3` earlier Mac activations wrote the template's timeout and `quiet:` line, leaving any other menu to Omarchy's migrations. U-Boot keeps EFI variables the OS sets at runtime in RAM (`EFI_RT_VOLATILE_STORE`): `omarchy-mac-efi-vars.service` writes them to the variable file U-Boot names (`RTStorageVolatile`, from `VarToFile`) as the Mac shuts down, so `systemctl reboot --boot-loader-menu`, `bootctl` and `efibootmgr` changes reach the next boot as on x86. It does nothing where U-Boot names no file. multi-user.target pulls it in only from the next boot, so the recipe's scriptlet starts it on install and upgrade, and on upgrade also runs `limine-menu-defaults` on the live menu, since activation does not run again.
 
diff --git a/omarchy-mac-boot/files/usr/lib/omarchy/mac-boot/external-displays b/omarchy-mac-boot/files/usr/lib/omarchy/mac-boot/external-displays
index ec2becb..882e77c 100755
--- a/omarchy-mac-boot/files/usr/lib/omarchy/mac-boot/external-displays
+++ b/omarchy-mac-boot/files/usr/lib/omarchy/mac-boot/external-displays
@@ -6,14 +6,13 @@
 #               can see it: forces every connector but the built-in panel off,
 #               only while the splash runs, on a laptop whose lid is open
 #               (a shut lid, a desktop Mac or an unknown lid keeps them all)
-#   release     omarchy-mac-external-displays.service, after the splash quits
-#               and owner setup ends, before the display manager: turns them
-#               back on
+#   release     omarchy-mac-external-displays.service, once the splash is gone
+#               (whoever quit it) and owner setup ends: turns them back on
 #
 # "off" and "detect" in a connector's status set and clear the kernel's force;
 # neither sends a uevent, so release sends each card a synthetic change that
-# the udev rule makes a hotplug (HOTPLUG=1) for the display manager and
-# compositor. The kernel console keeps the heads it lit when the card came up,
+# the udev rule makes a hotplug (HOTPLUG=1) for a display manager or
+# compositor that is already running. The kernel console keeps the heads it lit when the card came up,
 # so an external display may wake to a black console instead of staying
 # asleep. A boot that never reaches multi-user.target (emergency, rescue)
 # keeps the held displays off for that session.
diff --git a/omarchy-mac-boot/files/usr/lib/systemd/system/omarchy-mac-external-displays.service b/omarchy-mac-boot/files/usr/lib/systemd/system/omarchy-mac-external-displays.service
index b0fc013..c0cbb81 100644
--- a/omarchy-mac-boot/files/usr/lib/systemd/system/omarchy-mac-external-displays.service
+++ b/omarchy-mac-boot/files/usr/lib/systemd/system/omarchy-mac-external-displays.service
@@ -1,12 +1,19 @@
 # Turns on the external displays a Mac held off while its boot splash ran on
-# the built-in screen: after the splash quits, which first boot holds until
-# it hands over, and after owner setup or a password reset on tty1 ends,
-# before the display manager starts. Static: pulled in by multi-user.target,
-# so an upgraded Mac needs no enable step.
+# the built-in screen: once the splash is gone, which first boot holds until
+# it hands over, and after owner setup or a password reset on tty1 ends.
+# plymouth-quit-wait.service finishes only when Plymouth has exited, whoever
+# quit it: plymouth-quit.service before the display manager starts, or, with
+# Omarchy's Plymouth handover, omarchy-plymouth-quit.service once the
+# compositor the display manager started has the display. The release is not
+# ordered before the display manager: with the handover that would make the
+# display manager wait for the splash, which waits for the compositor, until
+# the handover's fallback timer quits it. The release sends a hotplug, so a
+# display manager or compositor that is already up rescans and lights them.
+# Static: pulled in by multi-user.target, so an upgraded Mac needs no enable
+# step.
 [Unit]
 Description=Turn external displays on for the desktop
-After=plymouth-quit.service plymouth-quit-wait.service omarchy-provision-owner.service omarchy-drive-recover.service
-Before=display-manager.service sddm.service
+After=plymouth-quit.service plymouth-quit-wait.service omarchy-plymouth-quit.service omarchy-provision-owner.service omarchy-drive-recover.service
 
 [Service]
 Type=oneshot
diff --git a/omarchy-mac-boot/test/mac-external-displays-test.sh b/omarchy-mac-boot/test/mac-external-displays-test.sh
index 84a56b1..2ec8630 100644
--- a/omarchy-mac-boot/test/mac-external-displays-test.sh
+++ b/omarchy-mac-boot/test/mac-external-displays-test.sh
@@ -156,9 +156,12 @@ grep -Fxq 'ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card[0-9]*", ENV{DEVTYPE}==
   fail "the Apple display card is held as it appears"
 grep -Fxq 'ACTION=="change", SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card[0-9]*", ENV{SYNTH_ARG_OMARCHYMACDISPLAYS}=="1", ENV{HOTPLUG}="1"' "$RULES" ||
   fail "the release's synthetic change is a hotplug (aquamarine rescans on HOTPLUG=1 only)"
-grep -Fxq 'After=plymouth-quit.service plymouth-quit-wait.service omarchy-provision-owner.service omarchy-drive-recover.service' "$UNIT" ||
-  fail "the release waits for the splash, which first boot holds, and for owner setup or a password reset on tty1"
-grep -Fxq 'Before=display-manager.service sddm.service' "$UNIT" || fail "the release runs before the display manager"
+grep -Fxq 'After=plymouth-quit.service plymouth-quit-wait.service omarchy-plymouth-quit.service omarchy-provision-owner.service omarchy-drive-recover.service' "$UNIT" ||
+  fail "the release waits for the splash to be gone, whoever quits it, and for owner setup or a password reset on tty1"
+# Omarchy's Plymouth handover quits the splash from the display manager's
+# compositor, so ordering the release before the display manager is a cycle.
+! grep -Eq '^(Before|RequiredBy|WantedBy|Requires|Wants|BindsTo|PartOf|Upholds)=' "$UNIT" ||
+  fail "the release orders or pulls in nothing else (no Before=display-manager.service)"
 grep -Fxq 'ExecStart=/usr/lib/omarchy/mac-boot/external-displays release' "$UNIT" || fail "the unit runs the release"
 [[ $(readlink "$FILES/usr/lib/systemd/system/multi-user.target.wants/omarchy-mac-external-displays.service") == ../omarchy-mac-external-displays.service ]] ||
   fail "multi-user.target pulls the release in without an enable step"
